    The engine, under the Fair Core License: the rail (passports, Missions, proxy, model gateway, MCP server, connections, drop-offs, agent-to-agent), the pattern detectors with their built-in rules, the controls (policy engine, limits, held actions, reviews, approvals, the control socket), the record, the worker, and the self-managed packaging. STACK's hosted business (accounts and their pieces, billing, the skills marketplace and the Console glue) is not part of this repository; the engine reaches none of it except through the seams it declares (see docs/self-managed/README.md). Memory (the knowledge graph and its engine) is hosted only: it is part of the account, and the engine app is not exported. The STACK network's server side (installs, countersignatures, cross-company revocation, the detection and classify services, licence revocation) is STACK's paid hosted layer and is not exported either: the engine keeps only the client that calls it with a licence key.

